33
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:49,240
Okay, the first thing you definitely need to learn

34
00:01:46,119 --> 00:01:52,719
is the concept of a microcontroller itself.

35
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:56,200
What exactly is a microcontroller?

36
00:01:52,719 --> 00:01:59,399
We often say "microcontroller," but what does that actually mean?

37
00:01:56,200 --> 00:02:02,680
What is the concept behind it?

38
00:01:59,399 --> 00:02:06,719
A microcontroller is essentially a small computer.

39
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:08,440
If you look at the computer you have at home,

40
00:02:06,719 --> 00:02:12,319
or the laptop you use, inside it you have a CPU,

41
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:15,519
RAM, and ROM,

42
00:02:12,319 --> 00:02:17,599
and I will explain all of these in detail on the next slide.

43
00:02:15,519 --> 00:02:20,800
In a computer, these are separate components,

44
00:02:17,599 --> 00:02:24,280
but in a microcontroller,

45
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:29,360
all of these components are integrated

46
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:32,480
inside a single chip.

47
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:34,680
So a microcontroller essentially

48
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:40,080
is a small computer

49
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:45,200
with things such as a CPU and Flash memory

50
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:49,319
all integrated into one chip.

51
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:54,080
So this is the concept of a microcontroller:

52
00:02:49,319 --> 00:02:57,200
all of these components are inside one chip.

53
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:59,280
You need to pay attention to this concept

54
00:02:57,200 --> 00:03:01,640
and understand

55
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:05,360
what concept you are actually using.

56
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:05,360
Keep this in mind.

57
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:11,840
The next topic is STM32 and ARM. I will explain

58
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:14,080
these topics fully on the next slide.

59
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:18,040

60
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:20,720
What is STM32? What is ARM?

61
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:23,640
People often mix these concepts up.

62
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:26,519
What is Cortex-M? What is Cortex-MT? What is ST?

63
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:29,080
I have put all of these together in this course

64
00:03:26,519 --> 00:03:32,080
so that we can fully understand their relationship.

65
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:32,080

66
